Feature: Commanding from the app
  The commander app is the seat of a person. It shows the map of your team: the field, the
  towers as your team last saw them, your drones, and the enemy drones that your team sees or
  saw. The rest of the field is dark: that is the fog. The top bar shows the clock and the
  score of each team.

  To give an order, click a drone in the list of drones or on the map, or press its number; drag a
  box on the map to select several drones, and hold Shift to add to the selection. Then right-click
  a tower on the map, and the drones go to take it. Right-click anywhere else on the field, and the
  drones go there and circle. HOLD makes the drone circle where it is. HOME sends it back over its base.
  The list of drones shows the order that the server has for each drone. Until you give a drone
  an order, it circles over its base: HOME.

  When a drone is selected, the UNIT panel shows its details: a small icon of the drone and its
  basic numbers. They are its class, its weight on a tower, its mass, its speed, its altitude
  and its state. The icon is a quadcopter for a light drone, and a plane for a standard or a
  heavy drone.

  LOW makes the selected drone fly [[low]], along the lanes and below the treetops. Click LOW
  again, and the drone flies high. CAMERAS shows the picture from the camera of each of your
  drones, the same [[sensor feed]] that the ground station shows. Click a picture to select
  its drone.

  Expectation: The app takes the Blue seat
    When the commander joins the game
    Then the seat of the app is Blue
    And the towers on the app's map are 5

  Expectation: A click on a drone selects it
    When the commander selects the first Blue drone
    Then the selected drone is the first Blue drone

  Expectation: With no drone selected, there is no UNIT panel
    Given the selected drone is none
    Then the unit panel of the app is hidden

  Expectation: The UNIT panel shows the details of the selected drone
    Given the selected drone is the first Blue drone
    Then the unit panel of the app is shown
    And the class in the unit panel is standard
    And the mass in the unit panel is 1.1 kg

  Expectation: A right-click on a tower sends the selected drone to take it
    Given the selected drone is the first Blue drone
    When the commander sends the selected drone to the west tower
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower

  Expectation: HOLD makes the selected drone circle where it is
    Given the selected drone is the first Blue drone
    When the commander holds the selected drone
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is hold

  Expectation: HOME sends the selected drone back over its base
    Given the selected drone is the first Blue drone
    When the commander sends the selected drone home
    Then the order of the first Blue drone is go home

  Expectation: A drone sent to a tower that nobody fights for takes it
    One drone takes a neutral tower in 20 s, but it must take off and fly there first. From the
    Blue base to the west tower is about 690 m.

    Given the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    When the game runs for 2 minutes
    Then the west tower on the Blue map is held by Blue

  Expectation: The app flies its drones itself
    The app is the ground station of its team: it does not hand the game server an order to carry
    out. It puts each drone in AGENT mode and sends it its plan as MAVLink, through the air, as the
    ground station of a real drone does. The game server only plays the world.

    Given the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    When the game runs for 2 minutes
    Then the drones that the app flies in AGENT mode are at least 1

  Expectation: The map of the app shows its drones where their telemetry puts them
    The app does not get the places of its drones from the game server. Each drone sends its
    position in its telemetry, and the app builds the part of its map that shows its drones from
    those reports. A drone that the app has not heard from lately is shown dim, where the app last
    heard it, with the time since. The enemy drones on the map are the ones that the drones, the
    towers and the base report, never an enemy that nobody told the app about.

    Given the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    When the game runs for 2 minutes
    Then the position reports that the app heard from its drones are at least 10

  Expectation: The game server is the umpire of the app, and not its map
    The game server tells the app the clock, the score and the outcome of the game, and what the
    towers and the base of its team see. It does not tell the app where its drones are, and it
    does not hand it a map of its team: the app makes the map from the reports of its drones and of
    its sites, as a ground station of a real team does. In the field, a service that reads the
    drones' positions (Remote ID, or logs) is the umpire.

    Given the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    When the game runs for 2 minutes
    Then the maps of the game that the game server sent the app are 0

  Expectation: LOW makes the selected drone fly low
    Given the selected drone is the first Blue drone
    And the flight of the first Blue drone is high
    When the commander flies the selected drone low
    Then the flight of the first Blue drone is low

  Expectation: A drone that flies low along the lanes takes a tower
    The way along the lanes is longer than the straight line, and the drone flies below the
    treetops all the way. It does not hit a tree.

    Given the order of the first Blue drone is take the west tower
    And the flight of the first Blue drone is low
    When the game runs for 3 minutes
    Then the west tower on the Blue map is held by Blue

  Expectation: CAMERAS shows the camera of each drone
    The pictures come when the 3D view has loaded the valley. That takes some minutes after a
    game starts, and the game goes on meanwhile.

    When the commander waits for the cameras
    Then the camera feeds in the app are 5

  Expectation: A click on a camera selects its drone
    When the commander clicks the camera of the second Blue drone
    Then the selected drone is the second Blue drone
